<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Bridger returns four weeks after phacoemulsification of the right cataract and one week after his fall. He had his one-month check at the eye clinic this morning; the surgeon&apos;s checks at one day and one week were normal. He finished the steroid drops yesterday, the antibiotic drops three weeks ago, and missed no doses with the voice reminders. With the right eye he can see faces across the yard and the colors of his apples again; the left eye is still blurred. The eye clinic changed the right lens of his glasses after the fall, and the mismatch between the eyes is less, though he still takes the porch steps slowly and holds the new second handrail. His right wrist is much better and he has stopped the splint. His back pain is down to about 4 out of 10 after five weeks of physical therapy. He has not driven. The VF-14 vision questionnaire was read aloud to him this morning before the second operation. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Right eye</td><td>82 letters (about 20/25); pressure 14 mm Hg</td></tr><tr><td>Left eye</td><td>54 letters (about 20/80), unchanged</td></tr><tr><td>VF-14</td><td>58 out of 100, read aloud</td></tr><tr><td>Wrist</td><td>Pain much less; splint stopped</td></tr><tr><td>Back pain</td><td>4 out of 10</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.18"/>
    <code code="10187-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Review of systems Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Eyes</td><td>Positive</td><td>Right eye clear; left eye blurred; no pain, redness, flashes or floaters</td></tr><tr><td>Musculoskeletal</td><td>Positive</td><td>Wrist almost painless; back better; knees as before</td></tr><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>Negative</td><td>No dizziness, leg numbness or weakness</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>3 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

